   "evidence": "`W1p.exists_dist_preciseRepresentative_le` (InteriorMorrey.lean:131) states only the H\u00f6lder form with a local `eLpNorm` on `ball x (2 * dist x y)`. The PR reduces that form to the Lipschitz constant inline at UniformCompactness.lean ~lines 80-93, while the analogous sup bound was given its own lemma, `W1p.norm_preciseRepresentative_le`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Sobolev/W1p/UniformCompactness.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public lemma in `W1p/InteriorMorrey.lean`, next to `W1p.norm_preciseRepresentative_le`, stating `\u2203 C, 0 < C \u2227 \u2200 (u : W1p mu \u22a4 \u221e) x y, dist (pr u x) (pr u y) \u2264 C * \u2016W1p.gradient u\u2016 * dist x y` (or a `LipschitzWith` form). The equicontinuity branch then reduces to applying it with \u2016gradient u\u2016 \u2264 1.",
   "issue": "The equicontinuity branch proves inline that dist (preciseRepresentative u y) (preciseRepresentative u x) \u2264 C * \u2016gradient u\u2016 * dist y x for whole-space W^{1,\u221e}. It does this by specializing `W1p.exists_dist_preciseRepresentative_le` at p = \u221e, running `simp only [ENNReal.div_top, tsub_zero, ENNReal.toNNReal_one, NNReal.coe_one, Real.rpow_one]` to remove the H\u00f6lder exponent, then bounding the local gradient norm through the chain `toReal_eLpNorm_gradient_mono`/`Lp.norm_def`/`norm_gradient_le`. This reusable endpoint fact is buried in a private lemma.",
   "line": 77
  }
 ],
